# Development Roadmap

## Phase 1 – Camera Setup

- [x] Configure Raspberry Pi and USB webcam backends
- [x] Live OpenCV camera preview
- [x] Create fixed 3×3 scanning overlay

## Phase 2 – Colour Detection

- [x] Capture BGR and HSV values
- [x] Calibrate from the six centre stickers for each scan
- [x] Implement LAB nearest-reference colour classification
- [x] Detect all nine stickers on a face

## Phase 3 – Cube Representation

- [x] Scan and persist all six faces
- [x] Validate six colour counts
- [x] Report colour-count scan errors for rescanning

## Phase 4 – Cube Solver Integration

- [x] Integrate Kociemba for 3×3
- [x] Integrate the pinned NxNxN solver adapter for 2×2/4×4
- [x] Generate and display guided solving sequences
- [ ] Verify a scrambled 4×4 after its lookup tables are installed

## Phase 5 – Embedded Features

- [x] Implement Sense HAT integration with a non-hardware fallback
- [x] Implement SQLite history and a retryable sync outbox
- [x] Implement the PHP/MySQL API and dashboard
- [x] Bound camera and remote-sync background work
- [ ] Verify the complete system on the Raspberry Pi and separate LAMP host

## Phase 6 – Scanner Consolidation

- [x] Make the team LAB scanner the only live scanner
- [x] Retain `src/vision/face_scan.py` as a compatible launcher
- [x] Add 2×2/4×4 calibration, review, correction, and per-session evidence

